<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>spark-service</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink: #1c2430; --muted: #5b6573; --line: #d9dee5; --link: #1f5f8b; --bg: #ffffff; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --ink: #e6e9ee; --muted: #a3acb8; --line: #3a4350; --link: #8cc4ec; --bg: #161b22; }
  }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
         font: 17px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 36rem; padding: 4rem 1.5rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.6rem; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 1rem; font-weight: 700; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 0.4rem; }
  p, li { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--muted); }
  a { color: var(--link); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--link); outline-offset: 3px; }
  footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>spark-service</h1>
  <p class="lead">A private, single-user app that connects its owner's own Google
  account to the owner's personal automation. It is not offered to the public.</p>

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reads the owner's Google Contacts, read-only, to recognise people the owner
    already knows. It never adds, changes or deletes contacts.</li>
    <li>Creates files in the owner's Google Drive and updates only the files it
    created itself. It cannot see any other file in the Drive.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>How this app handles Google data is described in the
  <a href="privacy.html">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <footer>
    <a href="privacy.html">Privacy policy</a>
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
